[b]Pivot Momentum Structure[/b]

[b]What it does[/b]
Classifies HH/HL/LH/LL structure on confirmed price pivots, then checks the oscillator for agreement or divergence at those same points. Instead of comparing every new pivot only to whichever one happened immediately before it, the divergence/alignment engine searches a short window of recent same-type pivots, scanning backward from the most recent, and uses the first one that clears the quality gates — reducing false negatives where a small, irrelevant pivot would otherwise block a genuine divergence, without over-reaching into old, barely-related pivots.

[b]Oscillator[/b]
[list]
[*]RSI (default) — classic momentum oscillator, OB/OS 70/30
[*]WaveTrend — smoother cross-based oscillator, OB/OS ±60
[*]Stochastic RSI — fast %K/%D, OB/OS 80/20
[*]CCI — centered on 0, OB/OS ±100
[*]Fisher Transform — smoother than RSI, OB/OS ±1.5
[*]TSI — double-smoothed momentum, OB/OS ±25
[*]Williams %R — native −100..0 range, OB/OS −20/−80
[*]CMO (Chande Momentum Oscillator) — bounded ±100, symmetric, OB/OS ±50
[/list]

[b]Structure Matrix[/b]
[list]
[*]Price HH + Momentum LH → regular bearish divergence
[*]Price LL + Momentum HL → regular bullish divergence
[*]Price HL + Momentum LL → hidden bullish
[*]Price LH + Momentum HH → hidden bearish
[*]Price and momentum both HH or both HL → bullish momentum alignment
[*]Price and momentum both LH or both LL → bearish momentum alignment
[/list]

[b]Structure Presets[/b]
Scalping / Intraday / Swing (default) / Position / Major Structure set Pivot Left/Right, Min/Max Pivot Distance, and the ATR price filter together, based on the swing size you want to detect — or choose Custom for full manual control.

[b]Anchor Selection[/b]
[list]
[*]The HH/HL/LH/LL label always compares to the immediately preceding same-type pivot — standard swing terminology, always intuitive
[*]Divergence and momentum-alignment checks instead search up to the last 8 same-type pivots, scanning backward from the most recent, and use the first one that clears the price- and oscillator-difference gates — never farther back than necessary
[*]Optional "Local Extreme" oscillator anchor mode reads the oscillator's own local high/low near the price-pivot bar instead of its exact value on that bar. Default is "Exact Pivot Bar" — the value read exactly on the price-pivot bar, no search involved.
[/list]

[b]Divergence Quality Score[/b]
Every fired divergence gets an optional 0-100 score averaging pivot spacing, oscillator-difference magnitude (relative to the oscillator's own rolling volatility), extremity past the OB/OS boundary, and trend context. It's purely informational — it never filters or blocks a signal, only helps judge which setups are structurally stronger.

[b]Quality Filters[/b]
[list]
[*]Minimum and maximum bar distance between compared pivots
[*]Minimum price difference, measured in ATR at the pivot bar
[*]Minimum oscillator difference — as a percentage of the oscillator's reference range, as a multiple of its own rolling standard deviation, or off
[*]Optional extreme-zone requirement for regular divergences
[*]Optional near-equal-pivot handling for double top/bottom structures (only ever feeds a regular divergence, never hidden divergence or alignment)
[*]Optional Trend Context Filter — hidden bullish only fires above a Trend EMA, hidden bearish only below it, keeping continuation signals aligned with the prevailing trend instead of firing during chop
[/list]

[b]Visualization[/b]
[list]
[*]Oscillator pane: HH/HL/LH/LL labels at each price-pivot bar, colored by structure
[*]Divergence connector lines drawn between the actual anchor pivot and the current one, in the oscillator pane and, separately, on the main chart
[*]Optional pivot guide lines connecting consecutive same-type pivots
[*]Optional chart-overlay pivot labels
[*]Dashboard: oscillator type, last pivot type, current price structure, current momentum structure, latest event, its age in bars, and how many bars back the event's anchor pivot was
[/list]

[b]Pivot Confirmation Delay[/b]
Pivots need right-side confirmation bars before they resolve. Signals therefore confirm with that delay but are drawn back on the true pivot bar, so the chart reflects the correct historical position while alerts still fire in real time on confirmation.

[b]Alerts[/b]
Seven conditions: regular bullish/bearish divergence, hidden bullish/bearish divergence, bullish/bearish momentum alignment, and a combined "any divergence" alert.

